(FUN-23 — all eleven expressible types are legal as a declared
 `Return a <type>,` return type. Every definition below is accepted and
 every function is called. Two of the eleven cannot be RECEIVED by the
 `a <type> called X is <call>.` declaration form — `file` and `timer` —
 so those two are received with `Set` instead; see Discrepancy 6 and
 D6.vox for why. `Return a buffer, "ABC".` (a text literal in the return
 expression) yields an EMPTY buffer, so this probe returns a buffer
 variable instead — see Discrepancy 7 and D7.vox.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FUN-23.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   7
   2.5
   seven
   1
   3
   30
   ABC
   12
   2026
   text payload
   timer return received
)
